  "name": null,
  "problem": "Consider the following initial value problem for the functions $y=y(x),z=z(x):$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}=3x+2y-z,\\, & y(0)=5 \\\\ {z}^{′}=x-y+4z,\\, & z(0)=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method.\nWhat entries should be placed in the columns for $Δy$ and $Δz$ in the table below if the step size is $Δx=1?$\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ |  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  | {{field-2}} |\n\nTherefore, $y(1)≈$\n{{field-3}}\nand $z(1)≈$\n{{field-4}}.",
